  "decision_date": "14/04/2005",
  "description": "Demolition of existing building and erection of a three storey 3 bedroom house.",
  "site_name": "28",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "18/10/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW8 8EQ",
  "street_name": "Market Place",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "13/04/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - It is considered that this application for the demolition of the existing house and the erection of a three storey three bedroom dwelling house would not be detrimental to the character and appearance of the 'The Butts' Conservation Area or of the adjoining listed building. Moreover the proposal will not adversely affect the amenities of the adjoining and neighbouring properties.  On balance, the development is in accordance with Policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), ENV. B.2.2 (Conservation Areas) and B.2.5 (Development Affecting the Setting of Listed Building) of the London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan adopted December 2003.  It is considered that where the development is not compliant there are no undue adverse effects resulting from this.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority (before the building(s) is/are occupied/used).",
    "Condition : 5 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 6 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no windows/dormer windows [other than those expressly authorised by this permission] shall be constructed.",
    "Condition : 7 - The roof area of the extension hereby permitted shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further specific permission from the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority a plan indicating the position, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before [the use hereby permitted is commenced] or [before the building(s) is/are occupied] or [in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority].  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 9 - A method statement, for making good all external walls exposed after demolition of number 28 and any alterations to the flank wall of number 26 following construction of the new building, be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the commencement of works and the approved details shall be implemented and maintained thereafter.",
    "Condition : 10 - The finished floor levels of the new building shall be higher than 5.94 metres above Ordnance Datum (Newlyn), which is the statutory tidal defence.",
    "Condition : 11 - The construction of the site drainage system shall be carried out in accordance with details submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the development commences",
    "Condition : 12 - The proposed works shall be built in relation to the building in which it is attached (No.26) in accordance with the submitted drawings",
    "Condition : 13 - ."
  ],
